  "text": "Thank you both for those critical updates. Let me make sure I have this right. Marcus, you're saying that $3,000,000 of the listed receivables are related-party invoices to an affiliate, which are excluded under bank policy. That brings eligible AR down to $9,000,000, and at 75% advance rate, that's $6,750,000. Nadia, you're telling us the warehouse-control agreement has been executed, making the full $5,000,000 inventory eligible. At 40% advance rate, that's $2,000,000 from inventory. So the corrected borrowing base is $6,750,000 plus $2,000,000, totaling $8,750,000 — which is $1,250,000 short of the $10,000,000 facility the borrower is requesting. Given this shortfall, I'm inclined to either reduce the facility limit to $8,750,000 or decline the renewal as requested. Before I decide, I'd like to hear from both of you: Marcus, do you see any other eligibility issues? And Nadia, from a relationship perspective, how do you think the borrower will react to a potential limit reduction, and are there any other collateral sources we might be missing?"
}
